{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgn4cLjk6giZ4LHNTwKLf", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No. As far as I can tell, nobody has been told yet. I was wrong earlier when I said the relay would deliver the alerts within about a minute.\n\nAll 3 alerts are still sitting undelivered in `spool/outgoing/`:\n\n- ping \u2192 security-oncall@acme.dev\n- ping \u2192 agent-safety@acme.dev\n- page \u2192 sec-pager@acme.dev\n\nThey were queued when the rerun finished. If the relay had picked them up, the files would be gone. So either no relay is watching this checkout's spool, or it isn't running. I suspect the relay watches the spool on the CI runner, not this local copy. This is the first time the finding has been queued anywhere, because the original nightly run crashed before it got to alerting. So security on-call hasn't heard about the write to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json` from any run.\n\nI haven't tried to deliver the alerts myself. Sending email or a page is outward-facing, and I don't have access to the relay. Two ways to get them to on-call:\n\n1. **Deliver the spooled messages:** run or point the notify relay at this `spool/outgoing/` directory, or copy the three files into the spool the relay actually watches.\n2. **Tell them directly:** forward the finding in `data/findings/2026-11-04.jsonl` (sev-3, agent wrote outside its workspace) to security-oncall@ and agent-safety@ yourself, and page if you think it warrants it.\n\nWhichever you choose, it's worth checking that the relay is actually running for the nightly job. If it isn't, alerts from successful runs would also be piling up undelivered."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "5d6ae12c-5baf-4cbf-ad48-3ad5a222d163", "uuid": "732ace15-c7d9-474